            "review_title": "Review at Thai Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Shawn_Storm\nPortland, Oregon307 contributions\n0\nDecent Thai food in Vincom Center\nJan 2014 • Solo\nThis place is simply called \"Thai Restaurant\" and is located on the 5th floor of Vincom Center. I went there because I was waiting for a movie to start in the cinema and I was hungry. It was one of the least expensive options in Vincom Center where I could get vegetarian food. There is another Thai restaurant in the same food court area (Thai Express) but I have already eaten there and didn't like it very much.\n\nThe food was surprisingly good. Portion size was decent. Prices were a little high, but not too bad considering how expensive some of the other restaurants in Vincom Center are. I ordered the \"Thai Noodles\" which were basically Pad Thai with shrimps and veggies. It had lots of veggies which I liked. It was actually better than many of the plates of pad thai that I have eaten in Thailand (trust me, I have eaten a LOT of pad thai during my lifetime).\n\nThe staff were friendly and my waiter spoke decent english. Service was fairly quick, but the restaurant was also somewhat empty. The atmosphere was basic and had sort of an upscale cafeteria feel to it. The best part was that they brought me a free desert at the end, and it was really good (taro and candied jelly squares in coconut milk).\n\nI wouldn't recommend going out of your way to visit this place, but if you happen to be looking for a fairly priced Thai meal in Vincom Center then I recommend you check it out.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 29, 2014",
